hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1611","Narrated to us 'Abdul-Jabbar ibnul-'Ala', who said: Sufyan narrated to us, who said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, who said: I heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (RA) say:\n\nMu'adh (RA) used to pray the Salah with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), then he would return to his people and lead them in prayer. One night, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed the 'Isha' prayer. When Mu'adh (RA) returned to lead his people in prayer, he began reciting Surah Al-Baqarah. A man then separated from the congregation and prayed by himself. When he finished, he went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah! Mu'adh leads us in prayer after praying with you. You delayed the 'Isha' prayer last night"," and when he came to lead us"," he began reciting Surah Al-Baqarah. We are laborers who work with our hands and rely on our watering animals. He is making the prayer too long for us.\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Mu'adh (RA)"," \""Are you causing tribulation"," O Mu'adh? Recite such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah.\"" We asked 'Amr"," \""Did Abu Zubayr not say that he recited *Subḥāna ism rabbika* (Surah At-Takwir) and *Was-Samā’i waṭ-Ṭāriq* (Surah At-Tariq)?\""\n\n'Amr replied"," \""It is something like that.\""\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
